<p>In Azure AI Search, an index is your searchable data. It defines the structure of your data and the fields you can search on. You can learn more about <a class="group inline" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/search/search-what-is-an-index" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">indexing in Azure AI Search<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a> in the official documentation.</p>
<p>There are a few ways to create an index in Azure AI Search. You can use the Azure Portal, Azure CLI, or the Azure SDK.</p>
<p>For a quick start, you can use the Azure Portal, to create an index schema.</p>
