<p>You can use the <code>createSearchIndex</code> function to create the index schema in Azure AI Search. Note that you need to replace <code>YOUR_SEARCH_ENDPOINT</code> and <code>YOUR_ADMIN_API_KEY</code> with your Azure AI Search service endpoint and admin API key.</p>
<p>Run the function to create the index schema in Azure AI Search. You can verify the index creation in the Azure Portal under the &quot;Indexes&quot; section of your search service.</p>
<h3 id="adding-data-to-the-index" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>Adding Data to the Index</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#adding-data-to-the-index" aria-label="Link to Adding Data to the Index"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3>
<p>As of the time of writing, Azure AI Search does not support direct indexing from PostgreSQL, but to populate your index, you can use the Azure Search REST API to upload data to Azure AI Search or use the Azure SDK as well.</p>
<p>Alternatively, you can export data from PostgreSQL to <a class="group inline" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/search/search-blob-storage-integration" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Azure Blob Storage<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a> and then add the blob storage as a data source to Azure AI Search. This method is useful for large datasets or when you need to sync data periodically.</p>
